{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7553299","formula":"AuNaO₃S₂","hill":"AuNaO3S2","elements":["O","Na","S","Au"],"composition":{"O":3.0,"S":2.0,"Au":1.0,"Na":1.0},"names":{"en":"Sodium aurothiosulfate","ru":"Дитиосульфатоаурат(I) натрия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sodium aurothiosulfate, or sanocrysin, is the inorganic compound with the formula Na3[Au(S2O3)2]·2H2O. It is the trisodium salt of the coordination complex of gold(I), [Au(S2O3)2]3−. The dihydrate, which is colorless, crystallizes with two waters of crystallization. The compound has some medicinal properties as well as potential for hydrometallurgy.","ru":"Дитиосульфатоаурат(I) натрия — неорганическое соединение, соль металлов натрия и золота и тиосерной кислоты, формулой Na3Au(S2O3)2. При нормальных условиях представляет собой красно-коричневое твёрдое вещество."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":170028,"mass":332.09,"charge":0,"smiles":"[O-]S(=O)(=S)[O-].[Na+].[Au+]","inchikey":"PMXFJUYOBVSEGY-UHFFFAOYSA-L","iupac":"sodium;dioxido-oxo-sulfanylidene-lambda6-sulfane;gold(1+)","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"170028","atoms":7,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.193,"y":-0.455,"z":-0.168,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.086,"y":-0.165,"z":0.469,"el":"S"},{"x":-0.081,"y":-0.109,"z":1.925,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.126,"y":-1.932,"z":0.128,"el":"S"},{"x":-0.936,"y":0.806,"z":-0.209,"el":"O"},{"x":3.505,"y":-0.729,"z":-1.079,"el":"Na"},{"x":-2.468,"y":2.584,"z":-1.068,"el":"Au"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1.0],[1,2,2.0],[1,3,2.0],[1,4,1.0]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7553299","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_aurothiosulfate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (